Hall","instructors":["Cole, C"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":""}]},{"id":"GWS 357","title":"Literatures of the Displaced","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"70262","code":"A","type":"Lecture-Discussion","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Lecture-Discussion","days":["T","R"],"start":660,"end":740,"location":"103 1207 W Oregon","instructors":["de la Garza Valenzuela, J"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":""}]},{"id":"GWS 360","title":"Women and the Visual Arts","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"40427","code":"A","type":"Lecture","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Lecture","days":["T","R"],"start":840,"end":920,"location":"316 Art and Design Building","instructors":["Buttery, H"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":""}]},{"id":"GWS 361","title":"Gender and Women in East Asia","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"70707","code":"A","type":"Lecture-Discussion","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Lecture-Discussion","days":["T","R"],"start":690,"end":770,"location":"1051 Lincoln Hall","instructors":["Shao, D"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":""}]},{"id":"GWS 366","title":"Feminist Disability Studies","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"78715","code":"TB","type":"Lecture-Discussion","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Lecture-Discussion","days":["T","R"],"start":570,"end":650,"location":"W115 Turner Hall","instructors":["Beauchamp, T"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":""}]},{"id":"GWS 387","title":"History of Sexuality in U.S.","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"63265","code":"SS","type":"Lecture-Discussion","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Lecture-Discussion","days":["T","R"],"start":750,"end":830,"location":"214 Davenport Hall","instructors":["Somerville, S"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"Meets w/HIST 387 (CRN 63266, Sec. SS)"}]},{"id":"GWS 390","title":"Individual Study","creditHours":"0 TO 3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"10359","code":"","type":"Independent Study","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Independent Study","days":[],"start":null,"end":null,"location":"Location Pending","instructors":[]}],"restrictions":[],"note":""}]},{"id":"GWS 393","title":"Policing Latinx Immigrant Communities","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"78716","code":"DVB","type":"Lecture-Discussion","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Lecture-Discussion","days":["M","W"],"start":720,"end":800,"location":"111 Gregory Hall","instructors":["Vergara Bracamontes, D"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":""}]},{"id":"GWS 395","title":"Intermediate Topics GWS","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"51239","code":"EK","type":"Lecture-Discussion","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Lecture-Discussion","days":["T","R"],"start":660,"end":740,"location":"44 English Building","instructors":["Kramer, E"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"Topic: Meets with ANTH 352 (CRN: 75699), Language and Gender. The relationship between language and gender is complex, contentious, and often misunderstood. In this course, we explore the many connections between language and gender. Topics include what gender is and how it is socially and linguistically constituted; real and perceived differences — grammatical, phonological, conversational — in how men and women speak; how the ways we talk about gender shape the ways we think about gender; and how all of these things vary cross-culturally and cross-linguistically. This course focuses on the role of language in constructing and sustaining gender in different societies around the world. We will examine linguistic mechanisms of creating gender divisions and stereotypes, as well as remedying gender-related inequality. Overall, the course aims to challenge our received notions of what gender is and how language and gender are interconnected. Among the topics covered are: institutional language and power; gender identity and language use; ideologies of gender and language; cultural definitions of “masculinity” and “femininity” and their relationship to language use; language and desire; and the social construction of gender identities through linguistic performance."}]},{"id":"GWS 399","title":"GWS Internship","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"68616","code":"MK","type":"Internship","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Internship","days":[],"start":null,"end":null,"location":"Location Pending","instructors":["Khan, M"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":""}]},{"id":"GWS 409","title":"Women's Health","creditHours":"3 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"31276","code":"A","type":"Lecture-Discussion","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Lecture-Discussion","days":["T","R"],"start":750,"end":830,"location":"112 Huff Hall","instructors":["Gobin, R"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":"Some seats are held for majors, but others are open to the public. Additional seats will be released on December 10. Please contact the Department with any questions."}]},{"id":"GWS 415","title":"Africana Feminisms","creditHours":"3 OR 4 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"62163","code":"1","type":"Online","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Online","days":["F"],"start":540,"end":710,"location":"","instructors":["Harrison, F"]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign."],"note":""},{"crn":"62184","code":"G1","type":"Online","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Online","days":["F"],"start":540,"end":710,"location":"","instructors":["Harrison, F"]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign."],"note":""}]},{"id":"GWS 432","title":"Gender Communication","creditHours":"3 OR 4 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"37087","code":"1","type":"Lecture-Discussion","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Lecture-Discussion","days":["T","R"],"start":660,"end":740,"location":"1027 Lincoln Hall","instructors":["Giorgio, G"]}],"restrictions":[],"note":""}]},{"id":"GWS 435","title":"Commodifying Difference","creditHours":"3 OR 4 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"40446","code":"G","type":"Lecture-Discussion","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Lecture-Discussion","days":["T","R"],"start":840,"end":920,"location":"327 Gregory Hall","instructors":["Peoples, G"]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign."],"note":"An interdisciplinary examination of how racial, ethnic and gender difference is negotiated through media and popular culture, and how racial, ethnic and gendered communities use cultural forms to express identity and difference. Among the theoretical questions explored in the course are the politics of representation, ethnic/racial authenticity, cultural commodification and transnational popular culture. Some of the cultural forms examined are cultural festivals/parades, ethnic/race-based beauty pageants, cinematic and televisual texts and musical forms, such as Hip-Hop and Salsa."},{"crn":"40517","code":"U","type":"Lecture-Discussion","partOfTerm":"1","meetings":[{"type":"Lecture-Discussion","days":["T","R"],"start":840,"end":920,"location":"327 Gregory Hall","instructors":["Peoples, G"]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign."],"note":"An interdisciplinary examination of how racial, ethnic and gender difference is negotiated through media and popular culture, and how racial, ethnic and gendered communities use cultural forms to express identity and difference. Among the theoretical questions explored in the course are the politics of representation, ethnic/racial authenticity, cultural commodification and transnational popular culture. Some of the cultural forms examined are cultural festivals/parades, ethnic/race-based beauty pageants, cinematic and televisual texts and musical forms, such as Hip-Hop and Salsa."}]},{"id":"GWS 442","title":"Body, Culture & Society","creditHours":"3 OR 4 hours.","sections":[{"crn":"71641","code":"OG1","type":"Online","partOfTerm":"A","meetings":[{"type":"Online","days":[],"start":null,"end":null,"location":"","instructors":["Carlson, K"]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign."],"note":"1ST EIGHT WEEKS: Registration for this course will close at 12 PM (noon) on 